.nh
.TH "ORBIT" "1" "Aug 2026" "Orbit Developer Platform" "Orbit Platform Manual"

.SH NAME
.PP
orbit-repair - Attach .git to gitless workspace trees without overwriting files


.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBorbit repair [scope] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Clones each target to a temporary directory and copies .git into the existing
tree. Working files are never checkout -f or reset --hard.

.PP
Use this when orbit status reports "gitless". Repositories that already have
\&.git are skipped. Missing paths are cloned as with orbit init.

.PP
Scopes match orbit init / orbit status (default: all).


.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB--concurrency\fP=4
	Number of concurrent repair workers

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for repair

.PP
\fB--manifest\fP=""
	Path to workspace.yaml (default: /workspace.yaml)


.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBorbit(1)\fP
